            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients experience oral pain in ways that make an accurate diagnosis difficult. The same complaints can be caused by either dental or nonodontogenic diseases. The author systematically explores symptoms and etiologies to direct the health care provider to an accurate diagnosis and treatment.</AbstractText>
